## Context

PR1713 touches scripts/corpus_icf_stage2.py and scripts/corpus_rel_view.py,
which retain bespoke argument parsers. The scoped script-I/O rule requires
parse_io_args/validate_io and explicitly permits a follow-up when migrating
an existing multi-output dispatcher is not small. Both commands have several
established input/output options; changing that public API would widen ticket2010.
This narrow follow-up is authorized by the root review and preserves current
behavior until the migration is reviewed.

## Exit criteria

- Migrate both named CLI parsers to the shared script_io_args parser and
  validation helpers while preserving their established dispatch commands,
  multi-output directory contract and append-only table options.
- Add a targeted ratchet that fails if either named CLI again bypasses the
  shared parser/validation entry points; cover representative historical and
  faceted invocation behavior with meaningful argument-routing tests.
- Keep Stage1/frozen v2 scientific prompts, source proofs and membership rules
  unchanged; run the required gate for the shared script-I/O boundary change.

## Scope

Only the two named CLIs and their focused parser/ratchet tests. No new remote
transport or generic API rewrite. Reference ticket2010 and PR1713 for provenance.
